-- title:
--   Regular differentials of level N vanish at every cusp
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and write $A_N =$ [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) for the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by the analytic $j$-function together with the Fricke functions $\mathrm{fricke}\,N\,v$ for $0 \ne v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$. Let $K$ be a field that is simultaneously a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra and an $A_N$-algebra, compatibly (scalar tower), and that is a fraction field of $A_N$. Let $\omega \in \Omega_{K/\mathbb{C}}$ lie in [`AlgebraicCurve.regularDifferentials`](def/AlgebraicCurve_RegularDifferentials.html#L26), i.e. for every place $v$ of $K/\mathbb{C}$ — a valuation subring of $K$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, distinct from $K$, and a principal ideal ring — there is $f$ in that valuation subring with $\omega = f \cdot d t_v$, where $t_v$ is the chosen uniformiser of $v$. Let $F : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be a function representing $\omega$ as $F(\tau)\,d\tau$ in the following sense: whenever $a, b, c, e \in A_N$ with $b \ne 0$, $e \ne 0$ and $\omega = (a/b) \cdot d(c/e)$ in $\Omega_{K/\mathbb{C}}$ (images taken under $A_N \to K$), one has $F(\tau)\,b(\tau)\,e(\tau)^2 = a(\tau)\bigl(e(\tau)c'(\tau) - c(\tau)e'(\tau)\bigr)$ for all $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$, the derivatives being those of the functions transported to the complex plane. Then for every $\delta \in \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ the weight-$2$ slash $F \mid_2 \delta$ is zero at $i\infty$.
--
--   This is the assertion that a differential of the first kind on the modular curve of level $N$, read on the upper half-plane as $F(\tau)\,d\tau$, gives a function $F$ vanishing at every cusp, the cusps being the places of the function field obtained from the $q$-expansion valuations at $\delta \cdot i\infty$. It feeds the construction of an injective linear map from the regular differentials of the level-$N$ function field to weight-$2$ cusp forms, [`ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LevelN_isZeroAtImInfty_slash_of_mem_regularDifferentials.lean

